## What "AutoReason for Ads" Looks Like

Per pass, for one underperforming ad, run **5 fresh agents** with no shared context:

| Role | Sees | Produces |
|------|------|----------|
| **Incumbent (A)** | n/a — IS the input | Current ad: headline, primary text, description, CTA, image/video reference |
| **Critic** | Incumbent + last 30/90d performance + top 3 winning ads from same audience | Critique only — NO rewrites |
| **Author B** | Incumbent + critique | Adversarial revision (B) |
| **Synthesizer** | A and B with **randomized labels** | Merged version (AB) |
| **Judge panel (3)** | A, AB, B in **randomized order** with **randomized labels** | Borda-count vote (3/2/1). Conservative tiebreak: incumbent wins ties. |

Convergence: **k=2 consecutive A wins** (paper proved k=1 premature, k=3 wasteful, k=4 actively worse).

Author temperature **0.8**, judge temperature **0.3**. Don't ablate without reason — paper validated these.

## The Knowledge Layer (the part that actually matters)

The fresh agents are useless without business-grounded context. Wire these in:

- **Meta Ads Insights** (already in `scripts/ads/meta.py`) — last 90d for the ad set, broken down by audience, placement, time-of-day
- **Top-performing ads** for the brand (CTR, CPL ranking) — pull from same Meta API
- **Worst-performing ads** — same source — useful as negative examples
- **Customer reviews + interview transcripts** — for KaiCalls these live in Gmail (per [[crm_lives_in_gmail]] memory) and `/opt/cmo-analytics/data/`
- **Audience-segment notes** — KaiCalls = SMB owners w/ phone-heavy ops; not the same voice as BWK creators
- **Brand voice locks** — KaiCalls positioning is locked per memory: "the new business phone number with AI built in" — NOT receptionist, NOT answering service. The Critic should flag any draft that drifts off this.

## Model Choice

Use **Haiku 3.5** (or Haiku 4.5) for authors and judges. Per the paper, this is the AutoReason sweet spot — Sonnet is so strong it doesn't benefit, Llama 8B is too weak to generate useful diverse alternatives. Connor pays Anthropic; route through the standard `claude` SDK.

Keep author/judge prompts in YAML or markdown so they're auditable, not buried in Python f-strings.

## Smallest Weekend Deliverable

**Pilot scope:** ONE underperforming KaiCalls ad set, ~5 ad variations, single AutoReason loop run, output written to a Discord thread for human approval before any Meta upload.

Concrete:
1. Pick the lowest-CTR active KaiCalls ad set (`scripts/ads/meta.py` can rank them).
2. Run the AutoReason loop on it. Cap at 5 passes max.
3. Post the winner + the full pass-by-pass trace (incumbent, B, AB, judge votes, why each was rejected) to `#kai-calls` Discord channel for approval.
4. Connor approves manually → only then push to Meta as PAUSED.

**DO NOT** auto-upload. **DO NOT** send any customer email. Per memory `feedback_no_customer_outreach`: only Connor emails clients, this rule applies to all paying KaiCalls customers including BBB, Starr's, Pete.

## Files To Create (suggested layout)

```
kai-cmo-harness/scripts/ads/autoreason/
├── loop.py            # The 5-role tournament runner — keep <300 lines
├── prompts/
│   ├── critic.md
│   ├── author.md
│   ├── synthesizer.md
│   └── judge.md
├── knowledge.py       # Loaders for Meta perf, top/bottom ads, customer voice
├── trace.py           # Per-pass trace recording for Discord approval thread
└── README.md
```

The orchestrator that calls AutoReason should live OUTSIDE this dir (`scripts/ads/ad_loop.py` is the right caller). Keep `autoreason/` pure: it takes an artifact + knowledge bundle and returns a winner.

## Verify Before You Commit

- `pnpm` is not used here; this is Python. Use the existing venv pattern from `scripts/ads/ad_loop.py`.
- Run on the ad set you picked, with `--dry-run` first.
- Print the full trace (5 candidates × pass count) so Connor can verify the loop actually behaves like AutoReason and not single-pass-with-extra-steps.
- Diff the ad against KaiCalls positioning lock before showing to Connor — any draft that says "receptionist" or "answering service" is auto-rejected.

## Out of Scope for the Pilot

- Email loops (KaiCalls / BWK welcome sequences) — same pattern, do later.
- BWK product pages — no live broadcast, judges can't ground in reply rate.
- Auto-upload to Meta. Always paused, always Connor-approved first.
- Generalizing across brands. Pilot is KaiCalls-only.

## Done Definition

- One PR opened against `kai-cmo-harness` with the new `scripts/ads/autoreason/` dir
- Loop demonstrated on one real KaiCalls ad set, full trace posted to `#kai-calls`
- Connor reviews the trace and gives go/no-go on whether to wire the loop into `ad_loop.py` step 3 as the new default

If at any point the loop produces a draft that breaks brand positioning, stop and ask. Don't rationalize a violation as "the judges chose it" — the brand lock is non-negotiable.

